    a number U is the sum of each N such that
        a period is in section121 two persons section121Person1 property ownage
        and the section121 two persons section121Person1 date of sale or exchange is a date D
            and the begin of the period is a second date
            and a date M is 60 months after the second date
            and D <= M
            and the begin of the period is a fourth date
            and the end of the period is a fifth date
            and the fifth date is a number N days after the fourth date
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person1 date of sale or exchange is a date K
            and the end of the period is a date P
            and a date Q is 60 months after P
            and K >= Q
            and N = 0
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person1 date of sale or exchange is a date R
            and the end of the period is a date S
            and a date T is 60 months after S
            and T is N days after R
    and U >= 730.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person1_requirements_usage_met with provenance "(a) Exclusion":
the rule section121 two persons section121Person1 requirements usage met holds if
    a number U is the sum of each N such that
        a period is in section121 two persons section121Person1 property usage as principal residence
        and the section121 two persons section121Person1 date of sale or exchange is a date D
            and the begin of the period is a second date
            and a date M is 60 months after the second date
            and D <= M
            and the begin of the period is a fourth date
            and the end of the period is a fifth date
            and the fifth date is a number N days after the fourth date
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person1 date of sale or exchange is a date K
            and the end of the period is a date P
            and a date Q is 60 months after P
            and K >= Q
            and N = 0
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person1 date of sale or exchange is a date R
            and the end of the period is a date S
            and a date T is 60 months after S
            and T is N days after R
    and U >= 730.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person1_section_121_b_3_applies with provenance "(3) Application to only 1 sale or exchange every 2 years":
the rule section121 two persons section121Person1 section 121 b 3 applies holds if
    the section121 two persons section121Person1 other section 121 a sale is a text
    and the text is equal to "MostRecentSaleWhereSection121aApplied"
    and the section121 two persons section121Person1 date of sale or exchange is a date D
    and the section121 two persons section121Person1 other section 121 a sale MostRecentSaleWhereSection121aApplied date of sale or exchange is a second date
    and a date N is 24 months after the second date
    and D <= N.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_date_of_sale_or_exchange with provenance "Section 121":
the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date if
    the section121 two persons date of sale or exchange is the date.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_gain_cap with provenance "(1) In general":
the section121 two persons section121Person2 gain cap is an amount N if
    N = 250000.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_gain_from_sale_or_exchange_of_property with provenance "Section 121":
the section121 two persons section121Person2 gain from sale or exchange of property is an amount if
    the section121 two persons gain from sale or exchange of property is the amount.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_income_excluded_from_gross_income with provenance "(1) In general":
the section121 two persons section121Person2 income excluded from gross income is an amount if
    the section121 two persons section121Person2 income excluded from gross income uncapped is an amount N
    and the section121 two persons section121Person2 gain cap is an amount M
    and N >= M
    and the section121 two persons section121Person2 gain cap is the amount
    otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person2 income excluded from gross income uncapped is the amount.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_income_excluded_from_gross_income_uncapped with provenance "(a) Exclusion; (3) Application to only 1 sale or exchange every 2 years":
the section121 two persons section121Person2 income excluded from gross income uncapped is an amount N if
    the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 section 121 b 3 applies holds
    and N = 0
    otherwise the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 requirements met holds
    and the section121 two persons section121Person2 gain from sale or exchange of property is N
    otherwise N = 0.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_other_section_121a_sale with provenance "Section 121":
the section121 two persons section121Person2 other section 121 a sale is a text if
    the section121 two persons person2 other section 121 a sale is the text.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_other_section_121a_sale_MostRecentSaleWhereSection121aApplied_date_of_sale_or_exchange with provenance "Section 121":
the section121 two persons section121Person2 other section 121 a sale MostRecentSaleWhereSection121aApplied date of sale or exchange is a date if
    the section121 two persons person2 other section 121 a sale MostRecentSaleWhereSection121aApplied date of sale or exchange is the date.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_requirements_met with provenance "(a) Exclusion":
the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 requirements met holds if
    the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 requirements ownership met holds
    and the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 requirements usage met holds.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_requirements_ownership_met with provenance "(a) Exclusion":
the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 requirements ownership met holds if
    a number U is the sum of each N such that
        a period is in section121 two persons section121Person2 property ownage
        and the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date D
            and the begin of the period is a second date
            and a date M is 60 months after the second date
            and D <= M
            and the begin of the period is a fourth date
            and the end of the period is a fifth date
            and the fifth date is a number N days after the fourth date
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date K
            and the end of the period is a date P
            and a date Q is 60 months after P
            and K >= Q
            and N = 0
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date R
            and the end of the period is a date S
            and a date T is 60 months after S
            and T is N days after R
    and U >= 730.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_requirements_usage_met with provenance "(a) Exclusion":
the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 requirements usage met holds if
    a number U is the sum of each N such that
        a period is in section121 two persons section121Person2 property usage as principal residence
        and the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date D
            and the begin of the period is a second date
            and a date M is 60 months after the second date
            and D <= M
            and the begin of the period is a fourth date
            and the end of the period is a fifth date
            and the fifth date is a number N days after the fourth date
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date K
            and the end of the period is a date P
            and a date Q is 60 months after P
            and K >= Q
            and N = 0
            otherwise the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date R
            and the end of the period is a date S
            and a date T is 60 months after S
            and T is N days after R
    and U >= 730.

rule section121_two_persons_section121Person2_section_121_b_3_applies with provenance "(3) Application to only 1 sale or exchange every 2 years":
the rule section121 two persons section121Person2 section 121 b 3 applies holds if
    the section121 two persons section121Person2 other section 121 a sale is a text
    and the text is equal to "MostRecentSaleWhereSection121aApplied"
    and the section121 two persons section121Person2 date of sale or exchange is a date D
    and the section121 two persons section121Person2 other section 121 a sale MostRecentSaleWhereSection121aApplied date of sale or exchange is a second date
